## Models carried

| Model | Where it comes from | Introduced or first used here | Used again here | After the band |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| feelings faces | SEL K to 2 (kindergarten unit 2), with the 1 to 5 strength scale SEL 3 to 5 adds in grade 3; grade 6 adds the exact word among close ones (g6-sa-name-feelings), so the card becomes the feelings scale: a word plus how strong it is | Unit 2 (grown) | Units 3, 4, 10, 11, 13, 15, 16 | Grade 9 reads a pattern in the feelings and plans for it |
| calm-down steps | SEL K to 2 and SEL 3 to 5 (four steps, stop, breathe, name it, choose, with a menu of three body tools; the shared calm-down card, STANDARD section 7); grade 6 grows them to five, stop, breathe, name it, pick a tool, go on, with a menu of four tools matched to settings (g6-sm-calm-down) | Unit 3 (grown) | Units 10, 15 | Grade 9 builds and judges its own plan from the steps |
| stop-think-choose | SEL K to 2 and SEL 3 to 5 (four steps, stop, list two or three choices, think what each would cause, choose and check); units 1 and 2 use that form; grade 6 grows it to five steps, stop, list options, weigh each, choose, write the reason (g6-rds-careful-thinking) | Unit 1 (grade 5 form); unit 3 (grown) | Units 2, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 12, 13, 14, 18 | Grade 9 judges a whole decision process against a shortcut |
| talk turn card | SEL K to 2 and SEL 3 to 5 (four steps, listen, say back, ask a question, add your idea); grade 6 adds a first step, choose how to talk (in person, a call or a message) (g6-rel-talk-listen) | Unit 4 (grown) | Units 6, 7, 11, 17, 18 | Grade 9 plans and checks a whole talk with it |
| I-statement frame | SEL K to 2 and SEL 3 to 5, the shared I-statement (STANDARD section 7) in four parts, "I feel ___ when ___ because ___. I need ___." | Unit 4 | Units 6, 7, 8, 11, 14, 17, 18 | Carried into grades 9 to 12 talks, limits and repairs |
| problem size meter | SEL K to 2 and SEL 3 to 5 (tiny, small, medium, big, each with who to go to); grade 6 sizes new-school problems on it and picks the helper that fits | Unit 1 | Units 6, 11, 12, 17, 18 | Grade 9 builds a map of where help is |
| goal steps | SEL K to 2 and SEL 3 to 5 (four steps, goal, steps, block and plan, check; the shared goal card, STANDARD section 7, whose rungs health's goal-plan and PE's goal cycle also use) | Unit 1 | Units 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 15, 18 | Grade 9 designs a shared goal with its review |

New in this band and kept all band: the refusal options card (unit 4: a plain no, a no with a reason, a way out of the place; the refusal steps of STANDARD section 7), the fairness questions card (from SEL 3 to 5, turned on online and offline norms in unit 5), the who-is-affected map (unit 5, its reach widened to an online audience) and the upstander options card (unit 6: speak up, support the person afterward, get an adult, report online). Within each year a card is grown only in the unit named here and used unchanged after it.

## Units

| # | Year | Unit and compelling question | Days | Skills | Owned standards | Core link and routines | What students learn | Why this unit, here | Check set adds | Sensitive topics and teacher notes |
