ange (in person, a note, in front of others), chosen to suit the friend (SO5). Retrieval: the five-step stop-think-choose and the calm-down steps (unit 3), the feelings scale (unit 2). End-of-unit evidence: a written scenario page on unseen cases (the channel and why; the question before taking a side; the refusal that fits) and a refusal rehearsed against an unseen card. Carry it out: "choose how to talk" before a hard message, on the card at the board. Family activity: agree together one kind of talk that is better face to face than by message. Tools: the talk turn card, the I-statement frame, the refusal options card, the feelings scale, paper message threads. Curio Class writes the threads, cases, cards and page. Provisional cost for 30: about $10 printing. Begun here, owned in grade 8 (unit): CASEL.Relationship Skills.1 (17), CASEL.Relationship Skills.2 (17), CASEL.Relationship Skills.5 (17), CASEL.Relationship Skills.6 (14), CASEL.Social Awareness.1 (16), CASEL.Social Awareness.4 (16), CASEL.Social Awareness.3 (16), CASEL.Social Awareness.5 (17). | After the mid-year check, when the first friend groups of the year have formed and shifted; after unit 3 because a hard talk and a refusal start with the calm-down steps and the five-step card. Health unit 4 (weeks 11 to 14) comes first with the same three refusal options; this unit opens with them where the school runs health (Cross-subject). ELA 6 teaches narrator point of view later (unit 5); the bridge is in Cross-subject. Three groups and 11 sessions. Sessions 32 to 42 of the year, weeks 16 to 21. | Candidate: the message threads printed as plain text with no platform look; the refusal card checked against health unit 4's wording | No student names friends, who left whom, or their own group's changes. The teacher or a card plays the pressure (STANDARD section 3); no student plays the pusher. Message threads are invented and on paper. Care for a friend's hard week names "tell an adult" when the hard week is a wo