### Library

AASL.V.D.1 is taught with SM3 (units 1, 8 and 15), AASL.V.D.2 with SA8 (units 3, 10 and 15) and AASL.III.D.2 with RS4 (units 6, 7 and 18): no SEL unit waits on library. docs/courses/library/STANDARD.md section 4 and data/plans/library-excluded.csv place them in SEL. The grade 8 owner rows (g8-sm-stay-on-task, g8-sa-skills-grow, g8-rel-teamwork) and units 15 and 18 name them; they move into the rows' standard cells once scripts/progression.py accepts AASL ids for SEL (For the lead 3).

## For the lead

1. **Unit sizes.** q-fix-sel-1 followed exactly (four 11s, two 10s a year): the course-level checks are the Check and Respond of units 3 and 6, as SEL 3 to 5 grade 3 does; the 30-minute dose allows it, so the pilot's 11/8 was not needed.
2. **Check weeks.** Grades 6 and 7: school day 75 (week 15), respond 78 (week 16). Grade 8: day 78, respond 80 (week 16), off the grade 8 science check on day 75. Year-end: day 158, respond 160 (week 32, finals). CALENDAR.md's stagger-rule list names no break for this course; nothing was moved for other after-core subjects.
3. **AASL ids for SEL.** scripts/progression.py and scripts/frame.py reject AASL.V.D.1, V.D.2 and III.D.2 in sel.csv standard cells.
4. **Rows.** Row changes in the writer's report: the two grade 6 notes SEL 3 to 5 also flagged, the grade 6 calm-down note, and "Snap judgements" (US spelling, also in STANDARD section 3).
5. **Health 6 to 8 side.** Health unit 3 (weeks 7 to 10) uses the grade 5 four-step calm-down card, before SEL adds "go on"; health unit 26's shared-project note cannot hold (weeks 18 to 22 against SEL unit 18's 27 to 31); health's SEL table can drop "may come first" for units 1 and 2.
6. **PE 6 to 8 side.** Its Pending note (line 360) on this frame can now cite SEL units 3, 6, 7, 10, 18.
7. **Career 6 to 8 side.** Its Pending notes (lines 128 to 133, 143) can cite SEL units 13 to 18. SEL places values, interests, strengths, goal and teamwork after career units 1 and 2; career keeps its short versions. Pick: keep STANDARD section 3's grade 8 order.
8. **Neighbors.** SEL 3 to 5 and 9 to 12 frames match this frame's seams; computer science grades 6 and 7 are not written (Pending notes).
9. **Spanish family notes.** Eighteen notes need a translation agent's read; no brief exists.
10. **Supply ceiling.** None set for SEL; about $55 to $60 a year printing plus $5 to $10 in units 6, 12, 18 and $4 once (Cory's money call).
11. **Brown v. Board source.** Named, not read; the sensitivity agent reads it before units 9 and 16.

