"C:\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command "python -B -X utf8 -c \"import csv; from pathlib import Path; rows=list(csv.DictReader(Path('data/progressions/sel.csv').open(encoding='utf-8'))); print('COLUMNS',list(rows[0])); [print(r['skill_id']+' | '+r['standard']+' | '+r['notes']) for r in rows if r['grade']=='8']\"" in S:\CurioClass
 succeeded in 154ms:
COLUMNS ['strand', 'grade', 'skill_id', 'standard', 'assumes', 'hands_on', 'model_in', 'model_out', 'words', 'cross_subject', 'notes']
g8-rds-ask-questions | CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.1 | Unit 1, How I decide. The student questions two invented sources that disagree on a school issue, stays open while friends have already picked a side, and writes a choice and reason. Owner year for 6 to 8: openness kept when it costs standing with friends.
g8-rds-check-facts | CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.2 | Unit 1, How I decide. The student checks a fast-spreading invented rumor against facts and numbers before a deadline to respond, and chooses on the evidence when the popular view leans the other way, writing the reason. Owner year for 6 to 8: evidence weighed under time and social pressure.
g8-rds-think-ahead | CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.4 | Unit 1, How I decide. The student weighs short- and long-term costs of options in an invented case (quitting a team for more free time), chooses, and later judges the choice against how the story turns out. Owner year for 6 to 8: a choice where every option costs something.
g8-rds-careful-thinking | CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.5 | Unit 1, How I decide. The student runs stop-think-choose with a two-minute limit on an invented case, then reflects in writing on where the clock bent the thinking and what a longer pause would have changed. Owner year for 6 to 8: careful thinking against a clock.
g8-sa-feel-think-link | CASEL.Self-Awareness.5 | Unit 1, How I decide. The student fills the think-feel-do chain for a character pushed to decide fast (an invented group chat demanding an answer now), writes a thought that slows the chain, and chooses. Owner year for 6 to 8: the chain changed while pressure pushes. Teacher note: a thinking skill used on characters, not a treatment; no student is asked to test their own thoughts aloud.
g8-rds-who-is-affected | CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.7 | Unit 1, How I decide. The student maps who a choice affects near and far when it is popular with friends but costs another group, and writes the pick with the reason. Owner year for 6 to 8: weighing everyone affected when it costs popularity.
g8-sa-tell-truth | CASEL.Self-Awareness.4 | Unit 2, Values and integrity. The student chooses the true action in an invented case where honesty costs a team its win (a missed call in its favor), and names the value behind it and the price. Owner year for 6 to 8: honesty with a real loss attached. Checked on the invented case only, never on a student's own conduct.
g8-sa-who-i-am | CASEL.Self-Awareness.1 | Unit 2, Values and integrity. The student shows how an invented eighth grader keeps their values across groups that want different things, and chooses what to hold to when one group pushes. Owner year for 6 to 8: identity held under group pressure. Teacher note: invented character first; a student may make up their own; family and culture are never asked about by name in a check.
g8-sa-my-strengths | CASEL.Self-Awareness.2 | Unit 2, Values and integrity. The student plans how an invented character could use a strength where showing it costs something (being called a try-hard), and writes the choice and reason. Owner year for 6 to 8: a strength used despite a social cost. Teacher note: home languages and culture are welcome when offered, never asked about.
g8-sa-snap-judgments | CASEL.Self-Awareness.6 | Unit 2, Values and integrity. The student checks a snap judgment an invented friend group already shares about a new student, chooses a fair action though disagreeing costs standing, and writes the reason. Owner year for 6 to 8: a fair action chosen against a group's shared guess. Teacher note: invented cases only; the skill is noticing and checking one's own guesses, never blame of a group.
g8-rel-say-no | CASEL.Relationship Skills.6 | Unit 2, Values and integrity. The student rehearses the refusal options against a card character who adds a price (being left out of a weekend plan, an invented post mocking them), and writes an exit plan tied to their values. Owner year for 6 to 8: a no held when it costs. Teacher note: the teacher or a card plays the pressure; no student plays the one who pushes and no real classmate is named; substance, body-safety and dating topics are health's (health row g8-aod-refusal-and-driving takes the unsafe-ride case).
g8-soc-read-situation | CASEL.Social Awareness.7 | Unit 2, Values and integrity. The student reads an invented situation whose stakes rise (a game at the park turns into a dare), chooses on stop-think-choose whether to stay, change it or leave, and writes what each costs. Owner year for 6 to 8: reading a moment as the pressure climbs.
g8-sa-what-interests-me | CASEL.Self-Awareness.9 | Unit 2, Values and integrity. Privately the student weighs whether an interest is worth what it takes (dropping another activity, time with friends) and writes a purpose for keeping or dropping it. Owner year for 6 to 8: keep or drop weighed against real costs, in writing. Teacher note: the list stays with the student; it is checked only that the steps were followed, never for its content.
g8-sa-i-can-try | CASEL.Self-Awareness.7 | Unit 2, Values and integrity. The student plans how an invented character could take on a challenge where failing would be public (a solo at a concert), with two steps, a helper and what to do if it goes wrong, on the goal steps card. Owner year for 6 to 8: belief acted on when failure has a cost. Teacher note: the course never records a student's own answer; checks use the character's plan.
g8-sa-name-feelings | CASEL.Self-Awareness.3 | Unit 3, Stress, focus and rest. The student names and rates the feelings of an invented student through a heavy week (tests, a game, a family event), choosing exact words as the strength rises, and writes the clue for each. Owner year for 6 to 8: feelings named as pressure builds. Teacher note: checks name a character's feeling and its clue; no clinical words; a student's own feeling is never recorded.
g8-sa-skills-grow | CASEL.Self-Awareness.8 | Unit 3, Stress, focus and rest. The student plans practice for an invented skill when time is short, choosing among more practice, better practice and asking for help, and writes why rest belongs in the plan. Never belief alone. Owner year for 6 to 8: growth planned under a time cost. Also carries AASL.V.D.2 (skill grows with practice and help), placed in SEL by library (docs/courses/library/STANDARD.md section 4); it moves into the standard cell once scripts/progression.py accepts AASL ids for SEL.
g8-sm-big-feelings | CASEL.Self-Management.1 | Unit 3, Stress, focus and rest. In a high-stakes invented scene (a tryout, a public mistake), the student uses the calm-down steps, picks a response from options, rehearses the steps and the response in a short scene, and writes what reacting would cost and how to recover. Owner year for 6 to 8: a response chosen when the stakes are high, with a plan to recover.
g8-sm-calm-down | CASEL.Self-Management.2 | Unit 3, Stress, focus and rest. The student builds a weekly coping plan for an invented busy student that weighs sleep, screen time and practice, chooses tools from the menu, and writes what each choice costs. Owner year for 6 to 8: coping chosen when every option takes time. Teacher note: breathing, stretching and pausing as plain body skills, with no spiritual framing. Stress, sleep and mental health topics are health's (health rows g6-meh-stress-coping and g7-phw-sleep-habits-community), named in the teacher notes. Teacher note: if a student tells of harm or risk, follow health's steps (docs/courses/health/APPROACH.md, "If a student tells you something"): the school's reporting route and the counselor.
g8-sm-stay-on-task | CASEL.Self-Management.3 | Unit 3, Stress, focus and rest. The student keeps an invented long project on track through a week with a game and a group chat that will not quiet down, chooses what to put off and writes the cost, and makes a try-again plan for the hardest part of the project, chosen from options (try another way, break it smaller, ask for help) with the reason written. Owner year for 6 to 8: focus held against both time and friends, and through the hard part. Also carries AASL.V.D.1 (trying again when a task gets hard), placed in SEL by library (docs/courses/library/STANDARD.md section 4); it moves into the standard cell once scripts/progression.py accepts AASL ids for SEL.
g8-sm-plan-and-tidy | CASEL.Self-Management.5 | Unit 3, Stress, focus and rest. The student plans an invented week where commitments clash (homework, a team, a family chore), decides what to cut or move, and writes the cost of each choice. Owner year for 6 to 8: planning when not everything fits.
g8-soc-their-view | CASEL.Social Awareness.1 | Unit 4, Understanding others. The student states the view of an invented person whose values differ on a school issue well enough that the person would agree with the summary, even when friends mock that view. Owner year for 6 to 8: taking a view that costs something to take.
g8-soc-care-when-struggle | CASEL.Social Awareness.3 | Unit 4, Understanding others. The student plans care for an invented friend whose hard time goes on, including when caring costs time or the friend's annoyance, and when to bring in an adult. Owner year for 6 to 8: care kept up over time, with the point where an adult comes in. Teacher note: if a student tells of harm or risk, follow health's steps (docs/courses/health/APPROACH.md, "If a student tells you something"): the school's reporting route and the counselor. Crisis topics are health's (health row g8-meh-suicide-help).
g8-soc-read-feelings | CASEL.Social Awareness.4 | Unit 4, Understanding others. The student reads feelings in an invented group conversation where cues hide behind jokes and short replies, chooses among responses one that may cost a laugh but respects the person, and writes the reason. Owner year for 6 to 8: cues read under the group's laughter.
g8-soc-fair-rules | CASEL.Social Awareness.6 | Unit 4, Understanding others. The student uses the fairness questions on a settled case the courts have ruled on, names what changing the norm cost the people who did it, and sets beside it an invented school norm that someone would pay a price to change. Owner year for 6 to 8: the price of changing a norm, in settled history and in school. Teacher note: settled facts the courts have ruled on, taught with dignity; current political disputes are not SEL content. The history itself is social studies' (ss8-civil-rights-laws).
g8-rel-different-ways | CASEL.Relationship Skills.3 | Unit 4, Understanding others. In an invented team whose partners' habits clash with a deadline close, the student chooses how to find common ground and writes what each side gives up. Owner year for 6 to 8: respect kept when time is short. Teacher note: no student is asked to explain their own culture; customs come from stories and invented partners.
g8-soc-notice-good | CASEL.Social Awareness.2 | Unit 4, Understanding others. The student gives specific credit to an invented rival team or classmate even when it costs a little pride, and writes why it matters. Owner year for 6 to 8: credit given to a rival, at a cost to pride.
g8-soc-why-rules | CASEL.Social Awareness.8 | Unit 4, Understanding others. The student traces how an invented school system and an invented app each reward some behavior, names the pressure each puts on students, and writes one change and what it would cost. Owner year for 6 to 8: a school system and an online one weighed side by side, with the cost of a change. Teacher note: invented apps, accounts and posts only, never the student's own; no product names.
g8-rel-talk-listen | CASEL.Relationship Skills.1 | Unit 5, Communication and conflict. The student uses the talk turn card in an invented hard talk where speaking plainly may cost a friendship, choosing the channel and the words, and writes the reason. Owner year for 6 to 8: the channel and the words chosen when plain talk may cost a friendship.
