### Picked up from Social and Emotional Learning, Grades 6 to 8

Every grade 9 row assumes its grade 8 row, the owner year of SEL 6 to 8, taught the year before (its frame, docs/courses/social-and-emotional-learning-grades-6-to-8/frame.md, units 13 to 18 in grade 8, "Handed on to Social and Emotional Learning, Grades 9 to 12"). Each grade 9 unit opens with the grade 8 form as retrieval, never a "Given:" item, unless the school did not run SEL 6 to 8 or left the unit out (then the Leave-out bridge). The grade 8 forms of the cards the grade 9 rows build on (SEL 6 to 8, Models carried): the feelings scale (a word and how strong it is), the five calm-down steps (stop, breathe, name it, pick a tool, go on) with a menu of four tools matched to settings, the five-step stop-think-choose (stop, list options, weigh each, choose, write the reason), the talk turn card with its first step "choose how to talk", the four-part I-statement ("I feel ___ when ___ because ___. I need ___."), the problem size meter with who to go to, the four-step goal steps card, and the refusal options, fairness questions, who-is-affected map and upstander options cards.

